# FleetLink Review Checklist

**Complete this review BEFORE writing or modifying code.** Follow `implementation-workflow.mdc` first — read all rules in `.cursor/rules/`, then complete this checklist. State the review outcome in your plan or first implementation message.

## 1. Architecture Review

- [ ] Does this belong in an existing feature module, or does a new feature folder need to be created?
- [ ] Is the change in the correct layer (component / hook / service / controller / repository)?
- [ ] Will this create duplication? Can an existing utility, hook, or service be reused?
- [ ] Does the folder structure match `architecture-standards.mdc`?
- [ ] Is the solution the simplest one that satisfies the requirement?

## 2. Performance Review

- [ ] Will this cause unnecessary re-renders? (new object/array literals in render, missing `key`, unstable callbacks)
- [ ] Is a list involved? If yes → FlashList + pagination required.
- [ ] Is memoization (`memo`, `useMemo`, `useCallback`) needed, or premature?
- [ ] Are large assets or screens lazy-loaded?
- [ ] Is navigation caching appropriate (e.g., `detachInactiveScreens`)?

## 3. Loading State Review

- [ ] What does the user see while data loads? (skeleton/shimmer — not blank, not spinner-only)
- [ ] What does the user see when the list is empty?
- [ ] What does the user see on error? (message + retry action)
- [ ] What does the user see on success?
- [ ] Are optimistic updates appropriate for mutations?

## 4. Type Safety Review

- [ ] Are request and response types defined in shared or feature `types/` folders?
- [ ] Are API errors typed and handled?
- [ ] Are form values typed with React Hook Form generics?
- [ ] Is `any` avoided entirely?

## 5. Reusability Review

- [ ] Can UI use existing `Button`, `Input`, `Card`, `Modal`, or loading components?
- [ ] Can logic use an existing hook or service?
- [ ] If creating something new, will it be used in more than one place — or is inline code simpler?

## 6. API & State Review

- [ ] Server data → React Query only (no Zustand, no `useState` for fetched data)
- [ ] App/session state → Zustand only
- [ ] Form state → React Hook Form only
- [ ] API calls go through service layer + React Query hooks — never directly in components
- [ ] Query keys, invalidation, and cache times defined?

## 7. Backend Review (if server changes)

- [ ] Route → Controller → Service → Repository chain followed?
- [ ] Input validated with a validation layer (Zod/Joi) before the controller?
- [ ] Errors handled by centralized error middleware?
- [ ] No business logic in models or routes?
- [ ] Indexes considered for new query patterns?

## 8. Security Review (if auth/data changes)

- [ ] Inputs validated and sanitized on the server?
- [ ] Passwords hashed with bcrypt (never stored plain)?
- [ ] JWT access + refresh token flow respected?
- [ ] Sensitive tokens stored in MMKV (mobile), never AsyncStorage?
- [ ] Authorization checked in middleware/service — not just on the client?

## Review Output Template

When starting work, briefly state:

```
Review: [feature name]
Architecture: [layer + folder]
Performance: [list? memo? pagination?]
Loading states: [skeleton / empty / error / success plan]
Types: [key types involved]
Reusability: [existing components/hooks used or new ones justified]
State: [React Query / Zustand / RHF assignment]
```

## Block Implementation If

- Any checklist item is unresolved and would violate a rule
- The proposed solution adds abstraction without a second use case
- A screen would ship without all four UX states (loading, empty, error, success)
